      "body": "<!--e57a25ab6845829454e8d69fc972939a-->\n\nThe following sections might be updated with supplementary metadata relevant to reviewers and maintainers.\n\n<!--006a51241073e994b41acfe9ec718e94-->\n### Code Coverage & Benchmarks\nFor details see: https://corecheck.dev/bitcoin/bitcoin/pulls/36236.\n<!--021abf342d371248e50ceaed478a90ca-->\n### Reviews\nSee [the guideline](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#code-review) and [AI policy](https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/master/doc/AI_POLICY.md) for information on the review process.\nA summary of reviews will appear here.\n<!--5faf32d7da4f0f540f40219e4f7537a3-->\n### LLM Linter (✨ experimental)\n\n\n\nPossible places where named args for integral literals may be used (e.g. `func(x, /*named_arg=*/0)` in C++, and `func(x, named_arg=0)` in Python):\n\n- `findFirstBlockWithTimeAndHeight(start_time - TIMESTAMP_WINDOW, 0, FoundBlock().height(start_height))` in `src/wallet/rpc/backup.cpp`\n\n\n\n\nPossible places where comparison-specific test macros should replace generic comparisons:\n\n- [test/functional/wallet_importdescriptors.py] `assert result[\"info\"][\"scan_start_height\"] <= first_header[\"height\"]` -> use `assert_greater_than_or_equal(first_header[\"height\"], result[\"info\"][\"scan_start_height\"])`\n- [test/functional/wallet_importdescriptors.py] `assert node.pruneblockchain(funding_height) >= funding_height` -> use `assert_greater_than_or_equal(node.pruneblockchain(funding_height), funding_height)`\n\n\n\n<sup>2026-09-13 08:35:41</sup>\n",
